160" y2="166"/><circle cx="666.2" cy="160" r="8"/><text x="666.2" y="164" text-anchor="middle">5</text><title>c. 2150 BCE: Gudea rules a rich and powerful Lagash, builds and restores temples, campaigns against Anshan and leaves the Gudea cylinders.</title></g><g class="rf-ev"><line x1="740.0" x2="740.0" y1="160" y2="166"/><circle cx="740.0" cy="160" r="8"/><text x="740.0" y="164" text-anchor="middle">6</text><title>c. 2110 BCE: Ur-Nammu of Ur slays Nam-mahani, ensi of Lagash, ending the Second Dynasty; the Lagash state becomes the largest province of the Ur III empire.</title></g><text class="rf-axis" x="20" y="200">2500 BCE</text><text class="rf-axis" x="740" y="200" text-anchor="end">2110 BCE</text></svg><figcaption>Relative power on the Institute's 0–10 scale (each profile scaled to its own peak). Numbers mark the key events below.</figcaption></figure><ol class="rf-events"><li><span class="rf-year">c. 2520 BCE</span><span class="rf-text">The First Dynasty of Lagash begins; En-hegal is believed to be its first ruler, followed by Lugalshaengur, named an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ensi">ensi</a> of Lagash on a mace head of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesalim-of-kish">Mesilim</a>, king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kish">Kish</a>.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 2450 BCE</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eannatum">Eannatum</a> defeats the army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umma">Umma</a> over the fertile Gu'edena, the battle shown on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stele-of-the-vultures">Stele of the Vultures</a>.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 2300 BCE</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-of-akkad">Sargon of Akkad</a> lays waste the land from Lagash to the sea; his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rimush">Rimush</a> later reconquers the rebellious city, recording 8,049 killed and 5,460 enslaved at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ur">Ur</a> and Lagash.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 2260 BCE</span><span class="rf-text">Puzur-Mama declares Lagash independent after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shar-kali-sharri">Shar-Kali-Sharri</a>; the Second Dynasty begins.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 2150 BCE</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gudea">Gudea</a> rules a rich and powerful Lagash, builds and restores temples, campaigns against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anshan">Anshan</a> and leaves the Gudea cylinders.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 2110 BCE</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ur-nammu">Ur-Nammu</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ur">Ur</a> slays Nam-mahani, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ensi">ensi</a> of Lagash, ending the Second Dynasty; the Lagash state becomes the largest province of the Ur III empire.</span></li></ol>
